<title>BELGIUM: SGB SAYS HAPPY WITH CURRENT PORTFOLIO.</title>
<headline>SGB SAYS HAPPY WITH CURRENT PORTFOLIO.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian holding company Societe Generale de Belgique SA (SGB) said on Wednesday it was happy with its current portfolio of six major holdings.</p>
<p>SGB chairman Etienne Davignon told a news conference he saw no reason to change it.  </p>
<p>The six core stakes are Tractebel , Generale Bank, Fortis AG , Union Miniere (UM) , Recticel and Sagem .</p>
<p>Earlier this month chief executive officer Philippe Liotier was quoted as saying the stakes in UM and Recticel &quot;were not forever.&quot;</p>
<p>&quot;Eternity is a philosophical concept,&quot; Davignon said. People had been wrong to conclude that UM and Recticel would be sold in the coming months. &quot;Our portfolio will continue as is.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
